{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041661-ministry-of-the-ruin","id":1041661,"title":"Ministry of the Ruin?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-31T20:19:40-08:00","id":1041661,"title":"Ministry of the Ruin?","content":"Ok so I know that only the Greater Ministries can truly claim Exarchal patronage (Ministry of Mammon aside), but I'm interested in what would a Ministry that was trying to exalt The Ruin and attract favor of the exarch of fate look like.<br /> <br /> How would they try to enforce and maintain the lie? what sort of people are they particularly interested in or look out for? without an archgenitor they couldn't have a prelacy but If they where to have individual Rote Specialties what do you think would fit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T20:26:00-08:00","id":1041664,"title":"","content":"For sake of the thread, here's the Ruin, 'Fate\u2019s Seal is the entropy that destryos dreams, relationships and even civilizations. Mystic destinies create new opportunities, but the Ruin ensures that people are skeptical and cynical about the opportunities ahead of them.'<br /> <br /> It does look tricky. I was thinking the only way you could get it is with some world-changing disaster. Y2K possibly maybe could have helped.<br /> <br /> But you know what's probably really good? Invoking the vibes of World of Darkness. Promoting belief in an end time, in constant entropy and portrayal of life as a zero-sum game. I suppose you could fake prophecies, scientific announcements about human evolution hitting a dead end, potential meteors coming to wreck the world, not immediately, but at some point within the future that you might survive live to. It would take a lot of work to do this sort of thing, at least to fake it.<br /> <br /> On a smaller scale it's probably easier. Countries can have leaders that get people behind them, promising big changes, then unashamedly and without even hiding it do the same thing their predecessors did. Take away people's cause for hope, because they'll know getting their hopes up is just a trap.<br /> <br /> Kinda going for an Omega Sanction vibe here, on the personal scale. It was used as metaphor for depression, but it's basically a torment by placing you within a series of 'lives' each more dreadful and inescapable than the next until one is broken. A punishing reincarnation until everything that was you was swallowed by oblivion.<br /> <br /> As it is they probably prey on the lower class and minorities that happen to have a lower status wherever they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-01-2017, 12:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T21:21:39-08:00","id":1041678,"title":"","content":"I would imagine that a Minstery of Ruin would be interested in, as mentioned above hypocritical leaders, economical regression and keep corrupting popular idols so that they can no longer serve as focal points. I also think that undermining all kinds of progress and show or &quot;show&quot; how these are only serlf-serving power grabs by a corrupt elite could work. This last should be doable on every level of human life.<br /> <br /> There should be many ways to prey on and break people's ambitions and dreams in economical and morale terms. Like for example how a project to lift a downthrodden neighborhood can be pushed to become a font for a criminal organization and make people in that neighborhood think that they can't do anything about their situation in life.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is to push empty solutions on vulnerable people. Like extrmist ideology and criminal life to make them think its the only way out but once they get there, its all empty of all hope or joy and find out they hope jumped into a cesspool of human suffering. That could affect both the people who take this &quot;chance&quot; themselves but also their close ones. And this solution could also open up to cooperation or &quot;coopertion&quot; with some other Ministries for those who serves, or wish to serve, Ruin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T01:44:11-08:00","id":1041740,"title":"","content":"The Fate arcana covers oaths among other things, so I've wondered about having a Fate ministry based on financial debt and legal systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:42:10-08:00","id":1042040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WelshBoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041661-ministry-of-the-ruin#post1041661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so I know that only the Greater Ministries can truly claim Exarchal patronage (Ministry of Mammon aside), but I'm interested in what would a Ministry that was trying to exalt The Ruin and attract favor of the exarch of fate look like.<br /> <br /> How would they try to enforce and maintain the lie? what sort of people are they particularly interested in or look out for? without an archgenitor they couldn't have a prelacy but If they where to have individual Rote Specialties what do you think would fit?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a side project to my current campaign, I've been working on homebrewing Ministries for the other Iron Seals. I've got the Ruin's down as the Ministry of Eschaton; they control through despair and the promise that all things amount to naught in the end. I wasn't sure about their Rote Specialties, but I think Survival, Intimidation and Subterfuge was one of the variations I considered.<br /> <br /> I considered that most of them are most interested in promoting fear of civilisation's fall, rather than speeding it along as their name suggests. Though there would probably be a sect of them who actually want to bring on the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:38:54-08:00","id":1042134,"title":"","content":"oo I've just come across an Indian religious sect that called Ajivika who came about same general time as Buddhism and lasted until 14th century. They believed in total determinism; that the entire universe was ordered according to a cosmic force called Niyati (Sanskrit for rule/destiny). According to the Ajivika Niyati meant that all things were entirely predetermined to the last detail and no amount of personal effort could change it. They were notoriously melancholic as a sect and practiced extreme asceticism and austerity. These guys sound entirely like what a Ministry of The Ruin would like to promote.<br /> <br /> I see these guys as becoming involved with loads of &quot;got talent&quot; and &quot;x factor&quot; style shows making sure few of them make any lasting improvement to their lives or attainment of fame. I could see them following up on lottery and competition winners and making sure that they regret ever entering...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/865-welshboi","name":"WelshBoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T12:44:19-08:00","id":1042555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041661-ministry-of-the-ruin?p=1041678#post1041678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine that a Minstery of Ruin would be interested in, as mentioned above hypocritical leaders, economical regression and keep corrupting popular idols so that they can no longer serve as focal points. I also think that undermining all kinds of progress and show or &quot;show&quot; how these are only serlf-serving power grabs by a corrupt elite could work. This last should be doable on every level of human life.<br /> <br /> There should be many ways to prey on and break people's ambitions and dreams in economical and morale terms. Like for example how a project to lift a downthrodden neighborhood can be pushed to become a font for a criminal organization and make people in that neighborhood think that they can't do anything about their situation in life.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is to push empty solutions on vulnerable people. Like extremist ideology and criminal life to make them think its the only way out but once they get there, its all empty of all hope or joy and find out they hope jumped into a cesspool of human suffering. That could affect both the people who take this &quot;chance&quot; themselves but also their close ones. And this solution could also open up to cooperation or &quot;coopertion&quot; with some other Ministries for those who serves, or wish to serve, Ruin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's a cycle:<br /> <br /> 1. The Silver Ladder gather resources (human and financial) for yet another utopian scheme.<br /> 2. One of the Greater Ministries finds a way to subvert said scheme.<br /> 3. The Ministry of Ruin publicises the outcome and accuses the pawns involved of corruption and/or hypocrisy.<br /> 4. Sleepers take down the pawns.<br /> 5. The Ministry of Ruin publishes the above as a triumph of the common man over the self-serving elite.<br /> 6. People celebrate and anticipate a better future.<br /> 7. The future sucks, in no small part because the community is operating in the absence of some of infrastructure developed to improve their lot.<br /> 8. The Ministry of Ruin pin the blame on the movement's failure on what's left of the Silver Ladder's pawns instead.<br /> 9. The Silver Ladder gather resources (human and financial) for yet another utopian scheme.<br /> <br /> Basically, follow what other mages are doing and send bits and pieces of the story to the Daily Mail.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T13:17:24-08:00","id":1042564,"title":"","content":"I've always imagined the Ruin as a mad dancer who draws the whole world toward eternal doom as she spiral around himself, taking a place almost satanic to the other Iron Seal- not like the Gate, but near enough the bottom that the Seers know that worshiping her as a patron is not the smartest thing to do. I've always imagined her Ministry as an fatalistic cult, driven by pure nihilism. You are bound to a fate not your own, living a story written by another. They enforce the Lie by making others fall into such hopelessness, making them believe that they can't change the paths which was laid to them. They were to a certain class and die as such. Where the Prophet would focus on the great people who make history move, the Ruin would focus on the grey people who work like cogs in the machine- secretaries and bureaucrats, protesters and anarchists, spies and assassins. They are the faceless mob who brings the revolution and manage the terror afterwards. They are never in the front, never taking the place of the protagonists- bu the mechanism which brings fourth the Deus Ex Machina.<br /> <br /> You never see the Ruin's climax to the plot before it's too late, but you always know that it is coming. That's the thing about good tragedies- you know how things would end, but you don't know how. You think the heroes are going to stop it, but each of their efforts just drives the story forward, toward their ultimate doom.<br /> <br /> Let the heroes take the front stage- they are the ones to die in the end. And when the applause would rise and everyone would cheer for the poisoned lovers or the stabbed knight, from behind the screen you would know that you fulfilled your role, and brought fourth the script just as your patron wrote it.<br /> <br /> yes, it was a fine tragedy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T23:26:14-08:00","id":1042840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041661-ministry-of-the-ruin?p=1042555#post1042555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's a cycle:<br /> <br /> 1. The Silver Ladder gather resources (human and financial) for yet another utopian scheme.<br /> 2. One of the Greater Ministries finds a way to subvert said scheme.<br /> 3. The Ministry of Ruin publicises the outcome and accuses the pawns involved of corruption and/or hypocrisy.<br /> 4. Sleepers take down the pawns.<br /> 5. The Ministry of Ruin publishes the above as a triumph of the common man over the self-serving elite.<br /> 6. People celebrate and anticipate a better future.<br /> 7. The future sucks, in no small part because the community is operating in the absence of some of infrastructure developed to improve their lot.<br /> 8. The Ministry of Ruin pin the blame on the movement's failure on what's left of the Silver Ladder's pawns instead.<br /> 9. The Silver Ladder gather resources (human and financial) for yet another utopian scheme.<br /> <br /> Basically, follow what other mages are doing and send bits and pieces of the story to the Daily Mail.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a Ministry of Ruin plan.<br /> <br /> The Ruin approves!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T07:58:29-08:00","id":1042949,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Yeah! Grant Morrison's take on the Omega Sanction and Anti-Life is a good source, I've used Darkseid's incarnation on Earth in comics like Mr. Miracle as inspiration for the Seers/Exarchs before in my Mage games. It depends on what level of bleak you and your players will enjoy, but a good depiction of the Ruin's Ministry would be people who kill hope. I'm sure you could find plenty of inspiration for that in 2016-17. A Ministry with media and government influence that gets people thinking on a grand scale instead of their own lives, and shows how that grand scale is without hope, but with just enough ambiguity and uncertainty to keep them interested in what happens next. Not only is there no chance for a better tomorrow, there was NEVER a chance, things were always going to be this way and always will. Good governance is impossible, global warming is unstoppable, natural disasters will end civilization within your lifetime and you can't do anything about it, etc.<br /> <br /> People who manipulate perception such that the present is projected forward and backward in time, differences are covered up, change is impossible and the people in charge were inevitably going to be there, regardless of their individual choices. Or for that matter, yours!<br /> <br /> (This way your players can have fun kicking their asses while explaining why there's hope and the possibility of a better future/present, shonen style)<br /> <br /> Give them a Prelacy, by all means. The merit explicitly invites you to make custom ones, it's intended to create unique characters, especially NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T12:33:52-08:00","id":1043092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041661-ministry-of-the-ruin?p=1042949#post1042949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Yeah! Grant Morrison's take on the Omega Sanction and Anti-Life is a good source, I've used Darkseid's incarnation on Earth in comics like Mr. Miracle as inspiration for the Seers/Exarchs before in my Mage games. It depends on what level of bleak you and your players will enjoy, but a good depiction of the Ruin's Ministry would be people who kill hope. I'm sure you could find plenty of inspiration for that in 2016-17. A Ministry with media and government influence that gets people thinking on a grand scale instead of their own lives, and shows how that grand scale is without hope, but with just enough ambiguity and uncertainty to keep them interested in what happens next. Not only is there no chance for a better tomorrow, there was NEVER a chance, things were always going to be this way and always will. Good governance is impossible, global warming is unstoppable, natural disasters will end civilization within your lifetime and you can't do anything about it, etc.<br /> <br /> People who manipulate perception such that the present is projected forward and backward in time, differences are covered up, change is impossible and the people in charge were inevitably going to be there, regardless of their individual choices. Or for that matter, yours!<br /> <br /> (This way your players can have fun kicking their asses while explaining why there's hope and the possibility of a better future/present, shonen style)<br /> <br /> Give them a Prelacy, by all means. The merit explicitly invites you to make custom ones, it's intended to create unique characters, especially NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that spreading threats of impending armageddon would be counterproductive. There would be fatalists, but deadlines push people into action. There would sleepers saying &quot;We need to get our shit together before [whatever]&quot; and no cost would be too high, because if they do nothing, they'll lose everything anyway. I say that it's better that they have some confidence that they will be able keep something precious to them that they don't want to risk losing by trying to change the world: a family, a job that just about covers the rent, a chance for salvation in the afterlife. They may say &quot;____ is going to fall apart in x years,&quot;, but they don't really believe that it will be gone altogether. They might not even go so far believing that the world is a bad place, but they do believe that's in a gradual decline.<br /> <br /> This all makes me think what a scourge some changeling courts must be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T14:58:08-08:00","id":1043165,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for a ministry dedicated to the Ruin who associated originally with the Indian caste system and social hierarchy. Formerly a great ministry which over hundreds of years spread from India to Europe and Asia. From there they spread with European colonialism with which they sought to encourage a dehumanizing hierarchy. And then they collapsed due to ideological* conflicts and a major schism leading many of their people to defect to the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> *They got into the habit of encouraging Awakening in those they thought were at the top of the social hierarchy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/801-grytorm","name":"Grytorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T15:14:23-08:00","id":1043182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1041661-ministry-of-the-ruin?p=1043092#post1043092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that spreading threats of impending armageddon would be counterproductive. There would be fatalists, but deadlines push people into action. There would sleepers saying &quot;We need to get our shit together before [whatever]&quot; and no cost would be too high, because if they do nothing, they'll lose everything anyway. I say that it's better that they have some confidence that they will be able keep something precious to them that they don't want to risk losing by trying to change the world: a family, a job that just about covers the rent, a chance for salvation in the afterlife. They may say &quot;____ is going to fall apart in x years,&quot;, but they don't really believe that it will be gone altogether. They might not even go so far believing that the world is a bad place, but they do believe that's in a gradual decline.<br /> <br /> This all makes me think what a scourge some changeling courts must be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't see a mention of deadlines. You can get by just fine with the doom, gloom and apocalypse talk for destroying hope without saying when it will happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}